# Field-wise factory rescue, called at the end of $restoreSettings.
# A setting that was NOT restored — absent from pRow because the package
# predates it, or because there is no package at all — is set to the
# factory value out of $settingsSpec. Everything that WAS restored is
# left alone: a value the user chose is never second-guessed here.
# Lists are skipped. An empty list cannot be told from a wrong one, and
# pbReset is the rescue for the container layout.
# Silent by design: one trace line only, there is no protocol at construct time.
# Returns the number of fields set.
Calculate spec as $cinst.$settingsSpec()
Calculate names as ''
Calculate healed as 0
For spec.$line from 1 to spec.$linecount step 1
	If spec.kind='setting'
		Calculate missing as kTrue
		If pRow.$colcount
			If pRow.$cols.$findname(spec.nm)
				Calculate missing as kFalse
			End If
		End If
		If missing
			Set reference defRef to $cclass.$cvardefs.$findname(spec.nm)
			If isclear(defRef)
			Else
				If defRef.$objtype=kList
				Else
					Do eval([spec.nm].$assign(spec.fac))
					Calculate healed as healed+1
					Calculate names as con(names,pick(len(names)=0,', ',''),spec.nm)
				End If
			End If
		End If
	End If
End For
If healed
	Send to trace log [con('[settings] ',healed,' field(s) set to factory at open: ',names)]
End If
Quit method healed